The change as described adds a single object at (0.8, 0.62), but the overlay shows many green marks labelled "1+" at various positions. The described add at x=0.8, y=0.62 would be near (409, 238) in pixels, which lands on the apple at approximately (403, 207) — already an existing instance in the scene. The change is ambiguous, and the image marks do not clearly match the stated coordinates.

The marks in the overlay lie at edges and partial apples (e.g., 487, 185; 497, 327), which do not match the single point (0.8, 0.62). Since the described add falls on an apple likely already in the draft, it is hard to justify.


